<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="65844" href="schedule/2017/spring/IE/598/65844.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2017" href="schedule/2017.xml">2017</calendarYear><term id="120171" href="schedule/2017/spring.xml">Spring 2017</term><subject id="IE" href="schedule/2017/spring/IE.xml">Industrial Engineering</subject><course id="598" href="schedule/2017/spring/IE/598.xml">Special Topics</course></parents><sectionNumber>AS </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Queuing Systems</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Prerequisite: IE 410 or an equivalent course on stochastic processes. This course is an introduction to queueing systems and their applications in engineering. Topics include both classical single-stage models and queueing networks. An emphasis will be placed on key methods, such as: imbedded Markov chains, PASTA property, reversibility, product-form stationary distributions, stochastic stability, asymptotic analysis.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2017-01-17Z</startDate><endDate>2017-05-03Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LEC">Lecture</type><start>05:00 PM</start><end>06:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>1131</roomNumber><buildingName>Siebel Center for Comp Sci</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Stolyar" firstName="A">Stolyar, A</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>